# A walked call reads the current graph (the book, #explicit-compilation: «the interpreter still performs the checks
# of every reached operation and call on the current graph»; «the walker may see it before native»). Under
# --walk-methods, once the body of target is rebound to the body of replacement, target() and a caller that calls it
# run the rebound body. Native runs are not observed here: before the turn ends their moment is unspecified.
# Entry 7; 81.. name the failing check.
fn: target () int
    return: 1
end: target
fn: replacement () int
    return: 1 + 1
end: replacement
fn: caller () int
    int: got target()
    return: (cast: (int) got)
end: caller
int: quote 11
int: src 12
sub: put_body ()
    quote\code := src\code
end: put_body
fn: m () int
    @: quote target target
    @: src replacement replacement
    if: target() != 1 || caller() != 1
        return: 81
    put_body()
    if: target() != 2
        return: 82
    if: caller() != 2
        return: 83
    return: 7
end: m
send: exit(exit_code: m(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
